1
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,290
[Unsoiled Starlight]

2
00:00:45,310 --> 00:00:47,040
[Episode 22]

3
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:47,500
[Adapted from Migu's novel
“Unsoiled Starlight” ]

4
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:47,960
[Original Writer: Shan Gu Jun]

5
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:50,780
Doesn't this one look good?

6
00:00:51,070 --> 00:00:52,240
No way, not that one.

7
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,220
This one's a no too.

8
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:55,560
Shu Tinglan.

9
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:57,410
Do you have any taste at all?

10
00:00:58,210 --> 00:00:59,860
Yours is the weird one.

11
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:01,060
When would you even wear that?

12
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:01,960
Tinglan.

13
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:05,820
Zhinan, you're here too.

14
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:06,600
Sorry.

15
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:08,300
I didn't know you had company.

16
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:14,450
Why are you here?

17
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,280
My wife ran away.

18
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:17,300
If I didn't come back,

19
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:18,830
she might leave me for good.

20
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:21,920
Don't be silly. I didn't leave you.

21
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:24,050
Then why won't you move back in?

22
00:01:24,310 --> 00:01:25,440
I just feel

23
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:27,000
more at home

24
00:01:27,110 --> 00:01:27,970
at my own place.

25
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:29,560
That place is yours too.

26
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,280
Like I said,

27
00:01:34,789 --> 00:01:36,280
you're the sole owner.

28
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,259
You still can't make big decisions

29
00:01:39,259 --> 00:01:40,860
without talking to me first.

30
00:01:41,830 --> 00:01:42,600
Got it.

31
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:45,280
Go talk to your friend.

32
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:46,320
I'll make dinner.

33
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:47,000
Okay.

34
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:52,720
Shu.

35
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:53,800
I take it back.

36
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:55,560
Your taste is fine.

37
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:57,280
A guy with his own dowry?

38
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:58,560
Now that's a keeper.

39
00:01:58,890 --> 00:01:59,670
See?

40
00:01:59,710 --> 00:02:01,370
We should get the one I picked.

41
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:03,320
I still don't like it.

42
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:03,960
Fine.

43
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:05,400
Let's just get both.

44
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:16,040
All right.

45
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,640
This is far enough.

46
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:18,640
My ride's waiting outside.

47
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:19,079
Okay.

48
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,400
Be safe.

49
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,300
Text me when you get home.

50
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:21,860
Okay.

51
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,440
Be safe.

52
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:24,920
Bye-bye.

53
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:26,040
You two go upstairs.

54
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:26,760
Text me when you're home.

55
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:27,600
Go on.

56
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:30,560
Come on.

57
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:32,000
Tinglan.

58
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,360
Let's go on our honeymoon.

59
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:37,880
Wait, really?

60
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:42,380
We fly out the day after tomorrow.

61
00:02:43,390 --> 00:02:44,920
You did it again?

62
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:47,660
I went ahead without asking.

63
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,400
But...

64
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,040
what about Mom?

65
00:02:52,079 --> 00:02:53,480
I'll set up video calls for her

66
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:54,730
the day after tomorrow.

67
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:55,440
And...

68
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:56,370
what about work?

69
00:02:57,170 --> 00:02:58,290
I'll handle your time off.

70
00:02:58,290 --> 00:02:59,079
You'll call Xiao?

71
00:02:59,079 --> 00:02:59,640
Yeah.

72
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:00,400
No.

73
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:01,410
You can't call her.

74
00:03:01,410 --> 00:03:02,320
Why not?

75
00:03:02,630 --> 00:03:03,470
No!

76
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:04,780
What's wrong with that?

77
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:05,780
People will talk.

78
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:09,040
Seriously.

79
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:49,720
You're not gonna

80
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:52,079
pack all night, are you?

81
00:03:53,329 --> 00:03:54,160
Stop packing.

82
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:01,350
I've got

83
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:02,310
the next two days

84
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:03,920
all planned out.

85
00:04:04,510 --> 00:04:06,240
Just wait. I've got surprises.

86
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:13,740
I'm so glad I have you.

87
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:16,519
Then...

88
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,800
Can I get a reward?

89
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:22,530
What kind of reward?

90
00:04:45,770 --> 00:04:46,320
Excuse me.

91
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:47,450
We booked this room.

92
00:04:49,110 --> 00:04:50,040
What's going on?

93
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:52,400
This is room 1101, right?

94
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:55,920
We booked it too.

95
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:01,760
I'm sorry.

96
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,200
There was an error in our system,

97
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,920
and the room was booked twice.

98
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,580
According to our records,

99
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,680
they booked it first.

100
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:10,000
We're very sorry.

101
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:13,640
So what can you do?

102
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:17,200
Could you

103
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,530
move us to another room?

104
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,160
I'm afraid not.

105
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:22,600
We're fully booked for two nights.

106
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,220
How about this?

107
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:25,960
If you pay us extra,

108
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:26,790
the room is yours.

109
00:05:26,790 --> 00:05:27,280
Sure.

110
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:28,050
How much?

111
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:28,970
How about...

112
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:29,780
What are you doing?

113
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:31,440
I don't want to switch hotels.

114
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:32,900
They're willing to pay extra.

115
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:34,830
You said this place was too pricey.

116
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:36,490
In that case,

117
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:37,600
could you please

118
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,159
process our refund?

119
00:05:40,150 --> 00:05:41,750
Can we go back to our room now?

120
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:42,400
Of course.

121
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:44,640
It's okay.

122
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:46,120
It doesn't matter where we stay.

123
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,120
What matters most

124
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:48,850
is that we're together.

125
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:50,920
Tinglan.

126
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:52,920
Hey.

127
00:05:53,159 --> 00:05:53,960
We meet again.

128
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:55,280
Yi Muyang.

129
00:05:55,570 --> 00:05:56,620
What are you doing here?

130
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:58,480
I guess fate brought us together.

131
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:02,640
The three of us.

132
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:03,520
Happy now?

133
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:04,760
Mr. Yi.

134
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:08,560
What happened?

135
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:11,380
Our room was double-booked.

136
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:12,710
We're getting a refund.

137
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:14,800
Leave it to me.

138
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:20,400
Move them to one of

139
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,620
our private rooms.

140
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:23,030
Tell them I approved it.

141
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,680
Why is he everywhere?

142
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:28,440
Sorry about that.

143
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:30,120
We'll upgrade you for free.

144
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:31,070
This room

145
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,710
usually isn't open for booking.

146
00:06:32,710 --> 00:06:33,409
That's great.

147
00:06:33,409 --> 00:06:34,610
Here's your room key.

148
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:36,820
Right this way.

149
00:06:37,070 --> 00:06:38,530
I'll show you to your room.

150
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:39,680
Let's go.

151
00:06:43,110 --> 00:06:44,480
Have their bags sent up.

152
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:46,400
Thank you so much.

153
00:06:46,490 --> 00:06:48,000
Dinner's on us tonight.

154
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:49,200
Sure.

155
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:51,000
Mr. Yi.

156
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:52,800
What is it?

157
00:06:53,210 --> 00:06:54,940
Your father is looking for you.

158
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:57,260
Tell him

159
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:58,440
I have plans later.

160
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:01,160
Looks like Yi Muyang is busy.

161
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,390
Let's head back to our room.

162
00:07:02,390 --> 00:07:02,880
Then...

163
00:07:03,510 --> 00:07:03,950
Wait.

164
00:07:03,970 --> 00:07:04,360
I...

165
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,640
Shouldn't we let him know first?

166
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:08,300
Your father insists you stay.

167
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:11,680
What for?

168
00:07:12,150 --> 00:07:12,960
He wants

169
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:14,570
you to play soccer with him.

170
00:07:14,950 --> 00:07:16,280
Soccer?

171
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,520
Not a chance.

172
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,480
Mrs. Cheng.

173
00:07:28,770 --> 00:07:31,480
We got an anonymous package
this morning.

174
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:32,320
Should I

175
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:33,400
throw it away?

176
00:07:35,250 --> 00:07:36,050
It's probably

177
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:37,720
another

178
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,159
wellness book

179
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:40,880
from his dad.

180
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:51,770
You can get back to work.

181
00:07:51,770 --> 00:07:52,640
Okay.

182
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:02,430
[Cardholder: Zhuo Yu'an]

183
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:14,250
I must've been working too much.

184
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,400
Even a walk in the park

185
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,530
feels relaxing now.

186
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,340
Shouldn't it be

187
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:21,820
being here with your fiance

188
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:22,880
that feels so good?

189
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:24,000
Right.

190
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,210
Look at all those birds.

191
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:33,250
Shu Tinglan.

192
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:36,200
You know what?

193
00:08:37,659 --> 00:08:39,590
There are things that scare me too.

194
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,520
The great Mr. Zhuo

195
00:08:43,610 --> 00:08:45,470
is actually afraid of something?

196
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:50,480
Guess what it is.

197
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:51,600
What is it?

198
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:52,640
Don't tell me

199
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:54,320
you're afraid I'll leave you.

200
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,200
Of course I am.

201
00:08:58,220 --> 00:08:59,280
Then what is it?

202
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:02,390
I'm afraid of water.

203
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:03,560
Water?

204
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:06,360
Let me tell you a story.

205
00:09:06,410 --> 00:09:06,960
Okay.

206
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:09,360
When I was a kid,

207
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:11,620
my grandpa was really strict.

208
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:13,600
He taught me manners

209
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:14,680
and how to behave.

210
00:09:14,950 --> 00:09:16,610
I didn't understand any of it.

211
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:18,160
I just wanted to have fun.

212
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,640
Back when I was a teenager,

213
00:09:20,940 --> 00:09:23,240
I went down to the river with some kids.

214
00:09:24,410 --> 00:09:25,440
One of them

215
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:26,480
pushed me in.

216
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:29,080
I was terrified.

217
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:30,960
I struggled in the water,

218
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,520
while they stood there laughing.

219
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:37,000
Then an old man came by

220
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,000
and pulled me out.

221
00:09:39,170 --> 00:09:40,130
Your parents

222
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:41,320
must've been so worried.

223
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,720
They must've felt awful.

224
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:47,480
Dad beat me with his belt

225
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:49,440
and locked me in his study.

226
00:09:50,010 --> 00:09:51,810
Mom fought with him for two days.

227
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:53,930
What happened next?

228
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:57,160
Then we had guests over.

229
00:09:57,910 --> 00:09:59,750
I cried and screamed in my room.

230
00:10:00,470 --> 00:10:02,200
My dad didn't want to lose face,

231
00:10:02,410 --> 00:10:03,640
so he let me out.

232
00:10:06,970 --> 00:10:08,630
You were so cute as a kid.

233
00:10:08,650 --> 00:10:10,580
You actually cried to get your way.

234
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:12,220
Doesn't matter how you do it.

235
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:14,400
What matters is that it worked.

236
00:10:16,730 --> 00:10:17,760
But it's okay.

237
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:19,280
We're grown-ups now.

238
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:21,400
The bad memories will fade.

239
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:23,400
Yeah.

240
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:27,930
The bad memories will fade.

241
00:10:41,450 --> 00:10:43,110
That vacation went by so fast.

242
00:10:43,230 --> 00:10:44,690
Then don't go back to work.

243
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:46,120
Quit my job?

244
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:48,900
I'll take care of you.

245
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:52,860
Where did you learn that cheesy line?

246
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:53,880
Surprise.

247
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:55,840
We meet again.

248
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:57,120
Hey.

249
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:58,360
Yi Muyang.

250
00:11:01,010 --> 00:11:01,920
That drink

251
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,150
is pretty strong.

252
00:11:03,150 --> 00:11:04,880
Want me to get you some juice?

253
00:11:06,550 --> 00:11:07,280
You two talk.

254
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:08,440
I'll get it.

255
00:11:14,830 --> 00:11:15,360
Tinglan.

256
00:11:15,990 --> 00:11:17,200
Want to see

257
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:18,520
how your cat is doing?

258
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:19,160
Sure.

259
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:20,600
I was just about to ask.

260
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:22,720
So cute.

261
00:11:23,170 --> 00:11:24,520
Has it gotten bigger?

262
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:25,360
Yeah.

263
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:26,890
I've taken great care of it.

264
00:11:26,890 --> 00:11:27,490
By the way,

265
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:28,920
what did you name it?

266
00:11:29,050 --> 00:11:30,160
I'm glad you asked.

267
00:11:31,050 --> 00:11:32,120
This one's Rice.

268
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:33,440
Hamburger.

269
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:34,320
Fries.

270
00:11:34,790 --> 00:11:35,680
Noodles.

271
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:37,400
Yi Tiaogou.

272
00:11:37,590 --> 00:11:38,680
A dog.

273
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:40,460
My last name is Yi.

274
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:41,780
Yi Tiaogou.

275
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:43,520
Why name it Yi Tiaogou?

276
00:11:43,670 --> 00:11:44,440
Because

277
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:45,800
everyone asks me why.

278
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:47,000
Isn't that fun?

279
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:50,670
What's so funny?

280
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:51,940
You look pretty happy.

281
00:11:52,870 --> 00:11:54,070
Which one do you want?

282
00:11:57,880 --> 00:11:58,440
Thanks.

283
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,590
Why did you treat him like that?

284
00:12:08,590 --> 00:12:09,520
Have mine.

285
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:10,370
It's fine.

286
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,160
I prefer water anyway.

287
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:15,840
Shu Tinglan.

288
00:12:16,550 --> 00:12:17,600
I'm jealous.

289
00:12:21,610 --> 00:12:22,670
You're back just in time.

290
00:12:22,670 --> 00:12:23,480
Sit here.

291
00:12:27,890 --> 00:12:29,800
We weren't talking about anything.

292
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,600
Remember that little black cat?

293
00:12:31,770 --> 00:12:33,480
We were just

294
00:12:35,550 --> 00:12:36,880
talking about its name.

295
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:40,440
What name?

296
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:44,400
Yi Tiaogou.

297
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:54,480
I go back to work tomorrow.
